# PONS $101 — TOKEN CREATION FACTORY

The PONS $101 Token Creation Factory is the technical execution-preparation layer of the ROB Lab.

Its purpose is to allow humans and authorized agents—including @hashwarlock-operated agents—to reproducibly prepare token-launch experiments, validate launch parameters, generate unsigned deployment payloads, observe public on-chain activity, calculate protocol-defined fees, and preserve the resulting evidence.

The system is deliberately divided into:

RESEARCH AUTOMATION

and

FINANCIAL AUTHORITY.

Agents automate research and preparation.

Humans retain authority over irreversible mainnet transactions.

==================================================
CORE PRINCIPLE
==================================================

AUTOMATE THE REPEATABLE.

PRESERVE THE IRREVERSIBLE FOR HUMAN APPROVAL.

The factory may automatically:

• create experiment manifests
• validate schemas
• check chain connectivity
• inspect contract state
• validate token metadata
• validate pair/reference assets
• inspect current fee configuration
• verify creator recipient configuration
• check launch eligibility
• estimate gas
• simulate transactions where supported
• generate unsigned calldata
• hash proposed payloads
• index launch events
• index trade events
• calculate fee components
• identify opening-window participation
• detect repeated behavioral patterns
• prepare after-action reviews
• export datasets
• generate reproducibility bundles

The factory does not independently:

• sign wallet transactions
• broadcast unauthorized launches
• buy newly launched tokens
• sell tokens
• generate wash volume
• target wallets
• spoof transactions
• manufacture market activity
• claim protocol revenue
• withdraw treasury assets
• change treasury recipients
• authorize public-good spending

