==================================================
BOT-LIKE BEHAVIOR ENGINE
==================================================

ROB classifies behavior.

It does not attempt to deanonymize users.

Possible signals include:

• extremely low launch-to-trade latency
• repeated first-block participation
• repeated transaction construction
• repeated gas strategy
• repeated trade sizing
• repeated behavior across unrelated launches
• repeated entry/exit sequencing
• repeated interaction with the same factory pattern
• recurring participation without public promotion

Each signal receives a research weight.

A score does not prove identity.

CLASSIFICATIONS

UNKNOWN

OPENING_WINDOW_PARTICIPANT

AUTOMATED_CANDIDATE

REPEATED_AUTOMATED_CANDIDATE

AUTOMATION_CONFIRMED

AUTOMATION_CONFIRMED requires evidence beyond timing alone.

